Dear list users,

I am back to using the NicheMapR after a long time. I found again this situation in which changing conditions that I considered important ( %shade and percent of surface acting as free water surface) had almost no impact in surface temperatures. I tried to follow Mike's advice below, but it seems there is still something I'm missing. Here goes a repeatable example. The algorithm uses the soil moisture model.

Thanks in advance,
Agus

# choose some scenarios
moist_surface=c(1,100)
maxshad=c(20,100)

# create a receiving vector
surftemp=vector()

# run scenarios
for(k in  1:length(moist_surface)){

  micro=try(micro_global(loc = c(-64.75,-15.25),
                         timeinterval=365,
                         nyears=1,
                         soiltype=6,
                         REFL= 0.1,
                         slope= 0,
                         aspect= 90,
                         DEP=c(0,1,2,5,7,10,20,30,50,80),
                         minshade= 10,
                         maxshade= maxshad[k],
                         RUF = 0.001,
                         PCTWET = moist_surface[k],
                         CMH2O = 1,
                         Usrhyt=1,
                         runmoist=1,
                         rainmult = .1,
                         SoilMoist_Init = c(0.4,0.4,0.4,0.4,0.4,0.4,1,1,1,1))
  )

  surftemp[k]=max(micro$soil[,3])

}
surftemp

